  "published": "2026-10-14T19:30:51.82Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Vali-Time v1.1.0 — add DurationStringParser (public parser extracted from ValiTime's duration-string grammar, reused by Vali-Duration), HumanizeCulture enum (En/Es, reused by Vali-Age), Constants.IsClampedMonthEnd helper (shared month-end-clamp detection, reused by ValiAge), and consolidate StartOfWeek/IsWeekend/IsWeekday into DateTimeExtensions as the single source of truth. No breaking changes.\n\n            Vali-Time v1.0.0 — initial release:\n            - Time unit conversions with full decimal precision: milliseconds, seconds, minutes, hours, days, weeks, months, and years.\n            - SumTimes: aggregate multiple time values across different units into a single result.\n            - FormatTime: human-readable output with configurable decimal places and CultureInfo support.\n            - GetBestUnit: automatic detection of the most appropriate time unit for a given value.\n            - ToTimeSpan: interoperability bridge to System.TimeSpan.\n            - Breakdown: decompose a duration into its constituent units (hours, minutes, seconds, milliseconds).\n            - ValiDate: date arithmetic (Add, Subtract, Diff), period boundaries (StartOf, EndOf), validations (IsBefore, IsAfter, IsWeekend, IsSamePeriod), and an extended Quarter API (QuarterName, ProgressInQuarter, DaysRemainingInQuarter, and more).\n            - Designed for seamless integration with .NET dependency injection via IValiTime and IValiDate interfaces.",
